From ba6efe679a21a00201d1ffae7f1d663f6d6bf0d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:56:03 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/32] Incremental: let metadata place a device by the arrays
 assembled

Incremental() picks the container for a device by the UUID that
getinfo_super() gave before the map was locked.  Metadata that records
no ID of its disk set - AMD RAIDXpert2, later in this series - can only
tell which container a device belongs to from the containers and devices
present, and its container UUID changes with the configuration (it comes
from the disks the newest configuration lists):

- two "mdadm -I" run together by udev both see no container of the set
  and create one each;
- a device that brings the container a newer configuration changes the
  container's UUID, and the map keeps the old one, so the next device of
  the set does not find the container.

Ask getinfo_super() again once the map is locked, so that devices
coming in together agree, and update the map entry of a container whose
UUID after load_container() differs.  It is getinfo_super() both times,
not uuid_from_super(): for an IMSM spare the two differ (uuid_zero,
which gathers the spares into one container, against the UUID of the
spare's own family).  The other formats give the same UUID from the
same superblock both times, and a container UUID that does not change
with the devices added, so nothing changes for them.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.2, AI models by Anthropic.
---
 Incremental.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Incremental.c b/Incremental.c
index 7a85cb90..b500b0bc 100644
--- a/Incremental.c
+++ b/Incremental.c
@@ -281,6 +281,14 @@ int Incremental(struct mddev_dev *devlist, struct context *c,
 	close(dfd);
 	dfd = -1;
 
+	/*
+	 * Metadata that records no ID of its array (AMD) finds the container
+	 * of a device by the containers and devices present: ask again now
+	 * that we hold the map lock and no other "mdadm -I" can add to them.
+	 * Ask getinfo_super(), as above: for an IMSM spare it gives
+	 * uuid_zero, uuid_from_super() the UUID of the spare's own family.
+	 */
+	st->ss->getinfo_super(st, &info, NULL);
 	mp = map_by_uuid(&map, info.uuid);
 	if (mp)
 		mdfd = open_dev(mp->devnm);
@@ -483,6 +491,20 @@ int Incremental(struct mddev_dev *devlist, struct context *c,
 			strcpy(devnm, fd2devnm(mdfd));
 		if (st->ss->load_container)
 			rv = st->ss->load_container(st, mdfd, NULL);
+		/*
+		 * The device may have brought the container newer metadata,
+		 * with another UUID (AMD derives it from the disks the newest
+		 * configuration lists): keep the map in step.
+		 */
+		if (!rv) {
+			struct mdinfo cinfo;
+
+			st->ss->getinfo_super(st, &cinfo, NULL);
+			if (memcmp(cinfo.uuid, info.uuid, sizeof(info.uuid)) != 0)
+				map_update(&map, fd2devnm(mdfd),
+					   info.text_version, cinfo.uuid,
+					   chosen_name);
+		}
 		udev_ready(sra);
 		sysfs_free(sra);
 		sra = NULL;
